  "ruleSetPolicy": "",
  "description": "The Employee Benefits Eligibility System determines whether an employee qualifies for specific benefits (e.g., health insurance, retirement plans, paid leave, bonuses) based on predefined criteria. This ensures fairness and compliance with company policies while optimizing resource allocation.\n\nThe system evaluates five critical factors:\n\nEmployment Type – Full-time, part-time, or contract-based.\nYears of Service – Determines if the employee meets the minimum tenure for certain benefits.\nPerformance Rating – Evaluates whether the employee qualifies for performance-based benefits.\nSalary Level – Some benefits may only be available to employees above a certain salary threshold.\nDepartment/Role – Some benefits may be specific to certain job levels or departments.\n\nThe eligibility decisions include Fully Eligible, Partially Eligible, or Not Eligible.",
